6502 CPU Emulator (WIP)
========================

A minimal, work-in-progress emulator for the MOS 6502 microprocessor,
written in C++. Based on the classic tutorial approach from
https://www.obelisk.me.uk/6502

STATUS

Early stage. Currently implements:
  - CPU reset
  - Memory read/write (64KB address space)
  - Byte and word fetch from program counter
  - Opcodes: LDA Immediate, LDA Zero Page, LDA Zero Page,X, JSR

Everything else (the rest of the 6502 instruction set, the stack
pointer actually decrementing on push, addressing modes beyond the
above) is not implemented yet.

FILES

  6502.cpp   - single source file, contains Mem, CPU, and main()

BUILD

  g++ -std=c++17 -Wall -Wextra -o 6502 6502.cpp

RUN

  ./6502

The included main() loads a tiny hardcoded program into memory:
a JSR to address 0x4242, which then runs LDA #0x84. After execution,
register A should hold 0x84.

DEBUGGING

Useful things to check when adding new opcodes:
  - Cycles is a signed int (s32). If an opcode's cycle count doesn't
    match what Execute() is told to run for, the while loop can run
    short or (if it were unsigned) wrap around and hang.
  - Watch PC and Cycles in gdb/pwndbg when a new opcode misbehaves:
        break CPU::Execute
        watch Cycles
        watch PC
  - Inspect raw memory directly:
        x/16xb mem.Data+0xFFFC

